cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Mandara Shell in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "Mandara Shell"
abstract: >-
  Mandara Shell is a native Linux Wayland desktop shell written in Rust on
  GPUI. It gives MangoWM, Niri, Hyprland and Umbriel a status bar, dynamic
  island, dock, launcher, sidebar, notifications, wallpaper engine, desktop
  widgets, lock screen, login manager and a live settings app, in one binary
  that uses under 100 MiB of RAM. Third-party plugins are sandboxed
  WebAssembly components, and almost every action is a documented
  command-line call with JSON replies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ahmad
    family-names: Hamdi
    alias: theHamdiz
repository-code: "https://github.com/theHamdiz/mandara"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - wayland
  - desktop shell
  - status bar
  - rust
  - gpui
  - hyprland
  - niri
  - mangowm
  - umbriel
  - webassembly plugins
